cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this software when using its formal proofs, constructions, or certificates."
type: software
title: "ARIADNE: Lean 4 Formalization of A∞ and Graceful Labelings for All Six- and Seven-Arm Spiders"
authors:
  - family-names: Sato
    given-names: Keisuke
    affiliation: "Independent researcher, Japan"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-4230-0268"
version: 1.0.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/stksk310/graceful-spider-lean"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - graceful labeling
  - spider trees
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
  - graph theory
  - proof assistants
abstract: >-
  ARIADNE provides Lean 4 proofs of the A∞ three-arm alpha-labeling theorem
  and graceful-labeling existence for every spider with six positive arm
  lengths and every spider with seven positive arm lengths. The formalization
  includes indexed spiders, exact vertex and edge-difference bijections,
  endpoint paths, shell/core fusion, unbounded core constructions, and
  all-integer case coverage. Finite witnesses are checked by Lean's kernel;
  the main theorems use only the standard axioms propext, Classical.choice,
  and Quot.sound. The release includes a Japanese proof manuscript and
  reproducibility evidence. Software and certificate data are Apache-2.0;
  manuscripts and prose documentation are CC BY 4.0.
